From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mckenna654 <mckenna654@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:13:28 +1100
Subject: Navigation fixes from a long arrow-only play-through; MODE option;
 respawn at last town

- Route data stores the exact stretch of each map edge per area, pooled.
- Paths keep off other doors and ladders, lead up to whoever blocks the way
  when there is no path around, and move on past people already dealt with.
- OPTION menu: BATTLE STYLE row replaced by MODE (Little / Junior / Classic).
- After losing, the player returns to the last town visited.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/include/little_trainers.h b/include/little_trainers.h
index 55fe1f47c..5b5ff9531 100644
--- a/include/little_trainers.h
+++ b/include/little_trainers.h
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ struct LtRules
     // Recovery and losing
     bool8 healAfterBattle;      // full party heal (HP, PP, status) when a battle ends
     bool8 noLossPenalty;        // losing a battle never costs money
+    bool8 autoRespawn;          // after losing, return to the last town visited (no need to have used its Centre)
 
     // Experience
     u8 expPercent;              // experience gained, in percent of the original (250 = x2.5)
@@ -130,9 +131,11 @@ void LT_DrawStartMenuIcon(u8 windowId, u8 startMenuItem, u8 y);
 // 8x8 heart tile for one slice of the HP bar with 0-8 of its pixels filled.
 const u8 *LT_HeartTile(u8 filledPixels);
 
-// Opens the story's puzzle gates for presets with simplePuzzles. Called on every map change,
-// before the map's own scripts decide what to draw.
+// Called on every map change, before the map's own scripts decide what to draw: opens the
+// story's puzzle gates (simplePuzzles) and moves the "return here after losing" point (autoRespawn).
+void LT_OnMapTransition(void);
 void LT_OpenPuzzleGates(void);
+void LT_SetRespawnForCurrentMap(void);  // src/heal_location.c
 
 // The "where do I go?" arrow (src/little_trainers_nav.c).
 void LT_Nav_Update(void);       // every frame on the field
